# e2e: a brush bigger or smaller than the Part (tester report, 0.13.3, macOS): a fresh default sphere (about 82k triangles),
# Symmetry X on. Bigger than the sphere: Inflate pulled shards, Move a spiky star, Sharp Crease wings, Clay a rocky crumple, Trim a
# crater; smaller: barely touched. Each brush, each Size, three strokes across the sphere: the mesh stays valid and nothing is flung
# out of the scene; at a Size under the sphere the stroke still moves it.
run new_sphere subdivisions=6
camera 0 0
expect_value symmetry_x == 1
snapshot_start

action brush.inflate
brush_size 400
snapshot
stroke 0.2 0.5 0.8 0.5
stroke 0.2 0.3 0.8 0.7
stroke 0.3 0.7 0.7 0.3
shot inflate-big
expect_mesh_valid
expect_value moved_max < 2.5
key ctrl+z
key ctrl+z
key ctrl+z
brush_size 150
snapshot
stroke 0.2 0.5 0.8 0.5
stroke 0.2 0.3 0.8 0.7
stroke 0.3 0.7 0.7 0.3
shot inflate-mid
expect_mesh_valid
expect_value moved > 20
key ctrl+z
key ctrl+z
key ctrl+z
brush_size 25
snapshot
stroke 0.2 0.5 0.8 0.5
stroke 0.2 0.3 0.8 0.7
stroke 0.3 0.7 0.7 0.3
shot inflate-small
expect_mesh_valid
expect_value moved > 20
key ctrl+z
key ctrl+z
key ctrl+z

